From: André Draszik <andre.draszik@linaro.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/crtc: fix detached fence name race and protect teardown

Backport the paired v3 drm_crtc dma_fence_ops fixes. Signaling can clear
fence->ops after a name callback has been selected inside an RCU read-side
section. Remove the racy BUG_ON and wait a grace period before CRTC cleanup
invalidates callback data. Both driver_name and timeline_name are covered.

Sources (also carried in Android common as bbea9e696f0c and 57acb869490b):
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260721-linux-drm_crtc_fix2-v3-1-afa8c71506e6@linaro.org/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260721-linux-drm_crtc_fix2-v3-2-afa8c71506e6@linaro.org/
Fixes: 541c8f2468b9 ("dma-buf: detach fence ops on signal v3")
Fixes: 6d6003c4b613 ("drm/fence: add fence timeline to drm_crtc")
Signed-off-by: André Draszik <andre.draszik@linaro.org>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
@@ -154,11 +154,8 @@
 #endif
 }
 
-static const struct dma_fence_ops drm_crtc_fence_ops;
-
 static struct drm_crtc *fence_to_crtc(struct dma_fence *fence)
 {
-	BUG_ON(rcu_access_pointer(fence->ops) != &drm_crtc_fence_ops);
 	return container_of(fence->extern_lock, struct drm_crtc, fence_lock);
 }
 
@@ -493,13 +490,22 @@
  * drm_crtc_cleanup - Clean up the core crtc usage
  * @crtc: CRTC to cleanup
  *
- * This function cleans up @crtc and removes it from the DRM mode setting
- * core. Note that the function does *not* free the crtc structure itself,
- * this is the responsibility of the caller.
+ * This function cleans up @crtc and removes it from the DRM mode setting core,
+ * after first waiting an RCU grace period to ensure @crtc->dev can safely be
+ * dereferenced by our dma_fence_ops.
+ *
+ * Note that the function does *not* free the crtc structure itself, this is the
+ * responsibility of the caller.
  */
 void drm_crtc_cleanup(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 {
 	struct drm_device *dev = crtc->dev;
+
+	/* Ensure our dma_fence_ops remain valid for an RCU grace period after
+	 * the fence is signaled. This is necessary because our dma_fence_ops
+	 * dereference crtc->dev.
+	 */
+	synchronize_rcu();
 
 	/* Note that the crtc_list is considered to be static; should we
 	 * remove the drm_crtc at runtime we would have to decrement all
